NAME
       modprobe - load or unload kernel modules

SYNOPSIS
       modprobe [-r] [-v] MODULE [PARAMETER=VALUE...]

DESCRIPTION
       Kernel modules are drivers and features that the kernel loads when it
       needs them (file systems, network cards, USB devices). modprobe loads a
       module by name, together with the modules it depends on. Usually this
       happens automatically; you need modprobe only for special cases.

       Settings for modules go in files under /etc/modprobe.d/; modules to
       load at every boot in /etc/modules-load.d/*.conf.

OPTIONS
       -r, --remove
              Unload the module (and unused modules it depended on).

       -v, --verbose
              Show what is done.

EXAMPLES
           modprobe -v xfs
           lsmod | grep xfs

SEE ALSO
       modinfo(8), lsmod(8)
